<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="text-align: right; margin: 0"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 14pt"><B>Valion Bio
Announces Reverse Stock Split</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>SAN ANTONIO, TX </B>&ndash; August 27,
2026 <I>&ndash;</I> Valion Bio, Inc. (Nasdaq: VBIO) (&ldquo;Valion Bio&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company) announced today that its Board
of Directors has declared a 1-for-25 reverse stock split of the Company&rsquo;s issued and outstanding shares of common stock. The
purpose of the reverse stock split is to bring the Company into compliance with the minimum bid price requirement for continued
listing on the Nasdaq Capital Market (&ldquo;Nasdaq&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The reverse stock split was approved by the stockholders
of the Company at a special meeting of the Company held on August 14, 2026. The reverse stock split will become effective on August 31,
2026 (the &ldquo;Effective Date&rdquo;) at 12:01 AM Eastern Time. The Company&rsquo;s common stock is expected to begin trading on a split-adjusted
basis when the markets open on August 31, 2026, under the current Nasdaq trading symbol &ldquo;VBIO.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The new CUSIP for the Company&rsquo;s common stock
following the reverse split will be 918942202.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As a result of the reverse stock split, every
25 shares of the Company&rsquo;s common stock issued and outstanding or held by the Company as treasury stock on the Effective Date will
be automatically reclassified into one new share of Company common stock. Proportionate adjustments will be made to the conversion and
exercise prices and the number of shares underlying the Company&rsquo;s preferred stock, outstanding warrants, equity awards and options,
and the number of shares reserved under the Company&rsquo;s amended and restated 2021 equity incentive plan, as amended.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The reverse stock split will not affect the number
of shares of preferred stock issued and outstanding, the number of shares of common stock or preferred stock authorized for issuance under
the Company&rsquo;s charter or the par value of the Company&rsquo;s common stock or preferred stock.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Each stockholder&rsquo;s percentage ownership
interest in the Company and proportional voting power will remain materially unchanged, except for changes and adjustments that result
from rounding fractional shares into whole shares. The rights and privileges of the holders of shares of common stock will be substantially
unaffected by the reverse stock split. No fractional shares will be issued as a result of the reverse stock split. Any fractional shares
of common stock resulting from the reverse stock split will be rounded up to the nearest whole share and no stockholders will receive
cash in lieu of fractional shares. The reverse stock split will affect all stockholders uniformly and will not alter any stockholder&rsquo;s
percentage interest in the Company, except to the extent that the reverse stock split would result in a stockholder owning more common
shares as a result of the rounding up to the next whole share for each fractional share.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Company&rsquo;s transfer agent, Odyssey Transfer
and Trust Company (&ldquo;Odyssey&rdquo;), is acting as the exchange agent for the reverse stock split. Stockholders who hold their shares
in book-entry form or through a bank, broker, or other nominee do not need to take any action in connection with the reverse stock split.
Stockholders of record will be receiving information from Odyssey regarding their common stock ownership post-reverse stock split.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As previously announced, the Company received
a notification letter from the Listing Qualifications Department of Nasdaq on March 19, 2026, notifying the Company that, because the
closing bid price of the Company&rsquo;s Common Stock was below $1.00 per share for 30 consecutive trading days, the Company was not currently
in compliance with the minimum bid price requirement. In accordance with Listing Rule 5810(c)(3)(A), the Company was provided 180 calendar
days, or until September 15, 2026, to regain compliance with the Rule. Although no guarantees can be offered, the Company believes that
this reverse stock split will allow it to regain compliance with the Nasdaq continued listing requirements and will enable the Company
to maintain its Nasdaq listing.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Additional information about the reverse stock
split and Valion can be accessed and viewed at the SEC&rsquo;s website, www.sec.gov, and at the Company&rsquo;s website, www.valionbio.com.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></P>

